scrollback & resizing need to be much more responsive
 - when resizing window with a program like htop open, program does not resize immediately

add support for user configuration via a config file (just a source we load on boot, can run arbitrary code; similar to stumpwm's config file).

support both libsixel and kitty graphics protocol;
  - both should start out as a lib here and eventually be able to be extracted into their own
    project, which others can then use
  - Kitty: placeholder placement ids (needs underline color in the grid); indexed-color
    images should follow palette changes
  - ghostty reports only scrolls that grow its scrollback; region and alternate-screen
    scrolls are inferred from the screen
  - 3bst stores a printed space as a blank cell, so a space written over a SIXEL
    cell does not erase it
  - images are decoded on the reader thread with the engine lock held (a 24 MB Kitty
    upload holds it ~0.4 s)
  - SIXEL: pixel aspect ratio (libsixel's decoder ignores it)
  - images under text (negative z) only on the Metal, GL and web backends

escape sequences (doc/escape-sequences.md):
  - backends report key presses only: the Kitty keyboard protocol cannot send release
    events or tell repeats apart
  - draw OSC 8 hyperlinks distinctly (underline on hover)
  - use the other OSC 133 marks (select a command's output, jump to failed commands)
  - styled and colored underlines (SGR 4:x, 58) in the engines and renderers
  - the web backend should follow OSC color changes

support drag and drop in both macos & X11 at the beginning

rename `backend` to frontend; idk why it is a `gui backend` as opposed to a `gui frontend`
engine can stay the same name though.
